# Normalize every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The Pulse regenerates files under data/ on every run
# and several checks in this change assert byte-identity between a
# regenerated file and its committed form (for example: "re-running with no
# state change produces a byte-identical queue", task 3.5). Node writes LF;
# if git checked those files out with CRLF on Windows, every regenerated
# file would differ from its committed blob on every line and those checks
# would be meaningless.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary payloads.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
